ADVISORY — CARRY-OVERS, NONE BLOCKING

  A1. Close step CS-2 is still open, and cascade 5 is what made it possible.
  `ClaudeCodeHooksOpts.sella` is now optional
  (packages/shim/src/hooks/claude-code.ts:93–102 strips the flag and its
  placeholder rather than substituting an empty string), so
  `claudeCodeHooksBlock({ studio: "studio" })` typechecks today where it did
  not in cascade 4b. It would not deep-equal the committed settings.json,
  however: the template's SessionStart/PreCompact entries invoke
  `bisellium hook-event context`, while the hand-authored file invokes plain
  `bisellium context`. Both inject the bundle; only `hook-event context`
  opens a receipt, and `hook-event start` in the same SessionStart group
  already does that, so the installed profile is functionally sound. The
  brief assigned CS-2 to the integrator, not to builder B, and behaviour 9's
  test is structural and passes either way. Take CS-2 in a later slot; it is
  not a defect of this opus and does not hold the pass.

  A2. The GLOSSARY.md front-matter seam is real and already on the record.
  `bisellium instructions --write` renders GLOSSARY.md without front matter,
  so it strips the docs-registry front matter W-019 added; commit 2f6c691
  already did exactly that. It is currently benign — the registry's field
  rules are scoped to `docs/*.md`
  (packages/cli/src/rules/docs.ts:67 returns early for README.md and
  GLOSSARY.md), so `check` is green and the tree is self-consistent — and it
  is already logged as a known gap in docs/SESSION-HANDOFF.md and in the
  dossier's cascade-5 row. Not chargeable to W-017: the brief told builder B
  in so many words to add no front matter and to let W-019 add it. Fixing it
  means deciding whether the generator preserves a registry header or the
  registry exempts generated files — a cross-opus decision, not a patch.

  A3. `report("commands.dir.listing", true, ...)` in instructions.test.ts is
  still a tautology that cannot fail, inflating the PASS count by one. Retro
  4b named it a pruning candidate and D-010 says a test that cannot fail is
  not evidence. It predates cascade 5, so it does not change this verdict;
  drop it on the next touch of that file, along with the now-unreachable
  `command.retro.exempted(W-018)` else-branch.

  A4. Evidence quality, not this opus: the lint certificate's redaction eats
  the information the log exists to carry. ci/W-017-lint-272d2d3b.log records
  `/********.test.ts` and `@********` where eslint printed
  `packages/cli/src/tick.test.ts` and `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars`, so
